Agreed.  I've also described it as how mean the unarmed monster is.

> If any of the following are true, the pet will not attack the monster.
>
> * the enemy XL is at least 2 levels higher than the pet

So the best term to use is the monster's XL.  A pet can attack a
monster with a higher XL because monster's only do reactive
hits on pets.  If a pet runs away the monster will not pursue and
keep trying to kill it.  If monsters did that nearly all pets would
die in the first several levels.  As it is there's a cycle of your pet
attacking for a while, backing off and healing for a while, then
resuming the attack.  It depends on pets healing faster than
most monsters or there would be a loop that never ends until
you call your pet to you.

> * 90% of the time when the enemy is a floating eye and can be seen by
> the pet
>
> * 90% of the time when the enemy is a gelatinous cube (9/10)

Both free action issues.

> * the "max passive damage" done by the enemy is greater than the pet's
> current HP
>
> * the enemy is a stoning monster and the pet is not stoning-resistant

Both issues where starting an attack would create a backlash
that doesn't look combat-like.

> * if the enemy is peaceful and there is no conflict on, and either

I was surpised to see this one.  I had thought that pets attack
peacefull monsters often.  I find plenty of item stacks in the mines.
Now I know my pet killed a monster that would have attacked me.

> ** the pet's current HP is less than 1/4 of the enemy' max HP

This explains why pets back off after some amount of combat.
It also explains why a monster armed with a nice weapon can
kill a pet.  One swing with a long sword can be enough to take
out that last quarter.  Also any monster that inflicts extremely
high hit points compared to its XL can kill a pet according to
this - kamakazie monsters of sorts that hit super hard but die
easily if their hit misses.

> ** or the enemy is MS_GUARDIAN (a guardian angel, I think)
> ** or the enemy is MS_LEADER (the quest leader, I think)
>
> So if it gets past ALL of those tests, then the pet will attack.
